[I] Compression algorithm library

[T] Zopfli is a compression library written in C by Google that performs
[T] very good, but slow, deflate, gzip or zlib compression. Its output stays
[T] compatible with standard decompressors, which makes it useful for data
[T] compressed once and served many times, and a zopfli command-line tool is
[T] included.

[U] https://github.com/google/zopfli

[A] Zopfli Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

